# Medical AI Services Configuration

## Overview
This file contains the API keys needed for the medical AI services (OCR, ACR, NLP) to process prescription images and audio.

## Required API Keys

### Google Cloud Platform
# Get your API key from: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# You need to enable:
# 1. Cloud Vision API (for OCR - text extraction from images)
# 2. Cloud Speech-to-Text API (for audio transcription)
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLOUD_API_KEY=YOUR_GOOGLE_CLOUD_API_KEY_HERE

### OCR Space (Fallback OCR Service)
# Free tier available at: https://ocr.space/ocrapi
# Use 'helloworld' for testing (limited requests) or get your own free key
EXPO_PUBLIC_OCR_SPACE_API_KEY=helloworld

## How to Set Up

### 1. Google Cloud Platform Setup (Recommended)
1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
2. Create a new project or select an existing one
3. Enable the following APIs:
   - Cloud Vision API
   - Cloud Speech-to-Text API
4. Go to "Credentials" and create an API key
5. Restrict the API key to only the APIs you enabled (optional but recommended)
6. Copy the API key and paste it above

### 2. OCR Space Setup (Fallback)
1. Go to https://ocr.space/ocrapi
2. Sign up for a free account (25,000 requests/month)
3. Copy your API key
4. Paste it above

## Testing
- You can use the default 'helloworld' key for OCR Space for initial testing
- Google Cloud Vision requires proper setup for production use
- The services will automatically fall back to OCR.space if Google Cloud Vision fails

## Important Notes
- Never commit this file with your actual API keys to version control
- Add `.env` to your `.gitignore` file
- For production, use environment variables from your hosting platform
- Free tier limits apply - monitor your usage
